{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.OptionELevelAcceptanceTest","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.OptionELevelAcceptanceTest","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.option_E_rejected_of_brackets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.option_E_rejected_of_brackets","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L276-L289","doc":"**Capstone.** For the actual trace curve of a fixed element: bracketing the\ntarget across the two admissible parameters forces the required parameter into\nthe open interval between them, and excludes both admissible parameters.\n\n`a` and `b` stand for the two admissible Markov parameters (`z_D` and `q`), `T`\nfor `Q_β / E₀`. The hypotheses are exactly what the probe measures per\ncandidate; the conclusion is what it reports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.continuous_traceCurve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.continuous_traceCurve","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L272-L274","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceCurve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceCurve","kind":"def","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L269-L270","doc":"The quadratic of `trAt_eq_quadratic`, as a function of `z` over `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.endpoints_not_roots_of_brackets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.endpoints_not_roots_of_brackets","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L260-L267","doc":"**The acceptance test, in the form a reader can apply.** A candidate that\nbrackets the target takes the target value at *neither* admissible parameter.\nNo continuity is needed for this half: the two strict inequalities are the\nwhole argument, which is what makes the test cheap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.brackets_forces_interior_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.brackets_forces_interior_root","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L251-L258","doc":"**Bracketing forces an interior root.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.conventionD_not_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.conventionD_not_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L222-L241","doc":"**Level 2 is not multiplicative.**\n\n`z_D = q³/(q²+1)` is neither eigenvalue: it is strictly below `q` and strictly\nabove `-q⁻¹`. So no unital multiplicative functional has `z_D` as its Markov\nparameter, and the argument that makes level 1 order-blind is unavailable at\nlevel 2.\n\n🛑 **Scope.** This *removes the obstruction*; it does **not** prove that level 2\nis order-sensitive. Non-multiplicativity permits sensitivity, it does not force\nit. That level 2 actually distinguishes two specific same-multiset words is a\nmeasurement (`qbeta_option_e_required_level_probe`, the interleaved vs\ngen-grouped models), not a consequence of this theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L219-L220","doc":"**The convention-D parameter is positive**, hence above `-q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_lt_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_lt_self","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L213-L217","doc":"**The convention-D parameter is strictly below `q`.** `q³/(q²+1) < q` for\nevery `q > 0`, since `q³ < q³ + q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.multiplicative_forces_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.multiplicative_forces_eigenvalue","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L200-L211","doc":"**Only two Markov parameters can be multiplicative.** If a unital\nmultiplicative functional sends the Hecke generator to `z`, then `z = q` or\n`z = -q⁻¹` — the two eigenvalues of `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hecke_image_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hecke_image_factor","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L193-L198","doc":"**The Hecke image equation factors.** Over any commutative ring, with\n`h = q - q⁻¹`, `z² - hz - 1 = (z - q)(z + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.augmentation_difference_order_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.augmentation_difference_order_blind","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L169-L178","doc":"**Order-blindness passes to a difference of two words.**\n\n`Δ = 𝓑_n - 𝓑_p` is a difference of two words. If each is re-ordered — which is\nwhat a different generator assignment or a different interleaving does — the\nvalue of a multiplicative functional on the difference is unchanged. So at\nlevel 1 those variants are not different candidates at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.monoidHom_order_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.monoidHom_order_blind","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L155-L167","doc":"**A multiplicative functional is blind to the order of a word.**\n\nThe commutativity that does the work is the **target's**, not the braid\nmonoid's. `w.prod = w'.prod` is *false* in `M`: a braid monoid is not\ncommutative, and a permuted word is a different braid. What is true is that `ε`\ncarries the product to a product of images, and *that* product lives in a\ncommutative ring where reordering is free. So order-blindness is a property of\nthe functional, not of the words — which is why it is level 1 that has it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.eminus_weight_at_level_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.eminus_weight_at_level_one","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L139-L145","doc":"**The `e⁻` weight at level 1 is `q³`.** With `h = q - q⁻¹`,\n`q·(h·q + 1) = q³` — so the trace at `z = q` really is the augmentation on the\nwhole basis, not merely on the short words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.coordSum_eq_trAt_one_of_eminus_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.coordSum_eq_trAt_one_of_eminus_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L122-L128","doc":"The two functionals agree exactly on elements whose `e⁻` coordinate\nvanishes — a property of the element, not a choice of convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.coordSum_sub_trAt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.coordSum_sub_trAt_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L114-L120","doc":"**The coordinate sum is not the trace at `z = 1`.** They differ by exactly\n`h` times the `e⁻` coordinate, because the trace weights `e⁻` by `z(hz+1)`,\nwhich is `h + 1` at `z = 1`, not `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.trAt_eq_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.trAt_eq_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L100-L112","doc":"**The trace is a quadratic in `z`, with explicit coefficients.**\n\nThis is the structural fact behind the acceptance test: for a *fixed* element\nthe map `z ↦ trAt h z v` is a quadratic, so requiring it to take a prescribed\nvalue does not leave a free choice of `z` — it determines `z` up to which of\ntwo roots. \"Which element\" and \"which functional\" are therefore one question. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.coordSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.coordSum","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L95-L98","doc":"The **coordinate sum**: every basis element weighted by `1`. This is the\nfunctional the corpus calls `net`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.trAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.trAt","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L89-L93","doc":"The Markov trace at parameter `z`, read off the basis weights\n`[1, z, z, z², z², z(hz+1)]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.eminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.eminus","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.Lplus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.Lplus","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.Lminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.Lminus","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.s1","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.s0","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.gamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.gamma","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFVec","kind":"structure","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OptionELevelAcceptanceTest.lean#L75-L83","doc":"Coordinates of an element of `H₃(q)` in the normal-form basis\n`[γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₋, L₊, e⁻]` used by the corpus's `Δ`-candidate census. ","signatureChunk":0}]}